MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adversarial review of #380 found the plan-first flow still dead-ended. Fixes:

F1 (HIGH): `forge plan` now REGISTERS the branch->issue linkage (create AND
--issue paths) via the kernel worktree registry, so a plan-created branch
resolves to its issue for kernel-authoritative stage state. Without it,
resolveActiveIssueId returned null on a plan branch and ship dead-ended.

F2+F3 (HIGH/MED): stage state is now COMPLETION-gated, not entry-gated. The
command runner records stage 'complete' only on handler SUCCESS (_registry.js);
enforceStageEntry gates ship/review on the predecessor being 'done' (not merely
entered), and lets stateless stages (plan/dev/validate/verify) RE-ENTER freely so
the dev<->validate rework loop never dead-ends. A single instantly-failing
validate no longer unlocks ship.

F4a: a UUID parsed from a branch name is bound only after verifying the issue
exists. F4c: `plan --issue B` on a branch already bound to issue A now ERRORS
(split-state guard) instead of warning. F5: `plan --issue` with no value ERRORS
instead of silently creating a duplicate. F6: dropped-write warnings go to stderr
even under FORGE_JSON=1 (never silent).

Quality: extracted helpers (enforceWithKernelState, enforceWithFileState,
resolveStageRuntimeHealth, isInlineStateProvided, resolveTrackingIssue) to keep
cognitive complexity under the A threshold; bindingless catch + optional chaining
for the SonarCloud new-code smells.

Tests: new test/workflow/plan-first-reachability.test.js drives the PLAN-CREATED
branch (no hand-wired linkage, non-UUID branch) plan->dev->validate->ship end to
end; added F2/F3 re-entry + completion-gate tests and F4c/F5 plan tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
